    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d1554">

                <pb facs="1236" n="1226" xml:id="pg1226"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">393.1121 Kanady, Dilmus/7–1249: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Consul General at Shanghai</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Cabot</hi>) <hi
                        rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State
                    </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Shanghai</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1949-07-12T18:00:00+08:00">July 12, 1949—6 p.
                            m.</date>
                        <lb/> [Received July 12—9:24 a. m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>2719. Consulate General has sent memorandum to Foreign Affairs Bureau re case
                    American citizen Dilmus Kanady arrested June 27 result minor traffic incident
                    June 26. He was given 48–hour jail sentence by police commissioner apparently
                    without evidence or hearing of any sort. No appeal permitted. Sentence served in
                    small cell without furniture or sanitary facilities.</p>
                <p>Memorandum to Foreign Affairs Bureau recites reported facts and inquires if
                    Kanady received trial or given right to appeal.</p>
                <p>Sent Department 2719, repeated Nanking 1528.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Cabot</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
